### Modifications to upstream files

`firmware/esp32_llm/esp32_llm.ino` — instrumentation only; inference kernels
unmodified:

1. Output-head row bound corrected from the compile-time constant `VOCAB_N`
   to `min(model.c.vocab, VOCAB_N)`, with the greedy-argmax bound matched.
   See "Instrumentation correction" in README.md.
2. Per-token activation buffer changed from a fixed-size static array to a
   heap allocation sized to the model's head width.
3. Boot banner extended to self-report firmware tag, CPU clock, flash clock
   and mode, and die temperature.
4. `N_GENERATE` and the watchdog feed interval made settable at build time.
5. GPIO window marker around the generation loop, for future power measurement.

The applied patch is reproducible via `tools/patch_fw.py`, which is idempotent
and reports which edits are already present.

## Original work

Copyright (c) 2026 Acramul Haque Kabir and Mohammad Mehedi Hasan Munna
MIT License

Recurrent language model stack, written for this study so that a second
architecture family could be measured under a protocol identical to the
transformer's:

    training/src/train_rnn.py       LSTM/GRU training, hidden-size solver
    training/src/export_rnn.py      int4 export + golden logits
    firmware/common/rnn.h           portable LSTM/GRU inference core
    firmware/host_verify/verify_rnn.c   C-vs-PyTorch verification
    firmware/esp32_rnn/esp32_rnn.ino    device sketch

The quantisation format (group-128 ragged int4 with fp16 scales) is
deliberately identical to the upstream transformer format so that the two
families share a packing implementation and can be compared without
format-related confounds.

Measurement and analysis:

    tools/campaign.py       transformer benchmark harness
    tools/rnn_campaign.py   recurrent benchmark harness
    tools/complete.py       supplementary experiment driver
    tools/patch_fw.py       firmware instrumentation patcher
    tools/analyze.py        analysis, figures, tables
    results/                measured data (648 runs)
    paper/                  write-up

